{"Title":"An Act to require liability insurance for gun ownership","BillNumber":"S1476","DocketNumber":"SD1440","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"MJB0","Name":"Michael J. Barrett","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/MJB0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T16:11:41.903"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"MJB0","Name":"Michael J. Barrett","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/MJB0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T16:11:41.9033333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S1476/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. Barrett, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 1476) of Michael J. Barrett for legislation to require liability insurance for gun ownership.  Public Safety and Homeland Security.","DocumentText":"\tChapter 140 of the General Laws is hereby amended by adding the following section:- \r\n\tSection 207. (a) Whoever possess, carries or owns a firearm, rifle or shotgun without a liability policy or bond or deposit required by the provisions of this chapter, which has not been provided and maintained in accordance therewith, shall be punished by a fine of not less than 500 nor more than 5,000 dollars or by imprisonment for not more than one year in a house of correction, or both such fine and imprisonment. This section shall not apply to a person who possesses a firearm, rifle or shotgun on a temporary basis while on the premises of a licensed gun club. \r\n\t(b) The commissioner of insurance shall promulgate regulations setting forth the minimum terms of liability insurance policies which shall satisfy the requirements of this section.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J22","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J22"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}